    {
      "number": 17,
      "id": "I_kwDORGnINM8AAAABO7nFEw",
      "title": "Comments from Russ Housley",
      "url": "https://github.com/teiclap/draft-porfiri-tsvwg-sctp-dtls-handshake/issues/17",
      "state": "OPEN",
      "author": "teiclap",
      "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Here are my thought on draft-porfiri-tsvwg-sctp-dtls-handshake.\n\nFirst, I want to note that draft-ietf-tls-extended-key-update, once it is finished, offers a better way to get fresh subsequent keys.  It can be used with resumption so that the TLS session does not need to be kept open.\n\nSection 1: Use the new TLS 1.3 RFC, not the original one.\n\nSection 3.2: It would be better to eliminate the double negative in the first sentence:\n\nIt is RECOMMENDED that only parameters marked as \"Y\" in the \"Recommended\" column of TLS registries are supported.\n\nSection 3.4: Is \"policy\" the right word? It is certainly quite different that certificate policies. I wonder if you are really asking for a configuration setting.  The rekey should happen whenever the time has passed _or_ the amount of data is about to be exceeded.\n\nSection 3.4: In the multi-homed situation, can more than one TLS session be needed by an endpoint?\n\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-31T06:05:27Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-31T06:05:27Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "comments": []
    }
